// The fourth lighthouse (bible 4.1, 6.1, 7.1). Room C.
// The lamp's inscription (environment first, style guide 6), and Warden-Sergeant Halvard's first hunt (6.3):
// the Guild finds her the moment the lamp is lit. No fight yet; a measuring. Halvard: Guild-formal, exact;
// his image is paces and counts. He never raises the lance here.

title: Lighthouse_Lamp
---
<<if has_flag("boss.lamp_keeper.defeated")>>
    Inscription: Fourth light of the chain. Lit for the flock, going south. #plant:5.6
    Inscription: Scratched under it, newer: "Still lit. Still here. Ask the light who it was for."
<<else>>
    Inscription: The housing is warm. Something up there is keeping the lamp.
<<endif>>
===

title: Lighthouse_Halvard_Hunt
---
Halvard: Journeyman Wren. Three paces. Stay in them.
Halvard: By the Guild's count you are missing. Missing does not carry a licence.
Halvard: Isolde Marr is dead by the same count. It was taken the morning after. #plant:5.2
-> A count isn't a survey.
    Halvard: No. A survey would have cost a day. The Guildmaster gave it an hour. #plant:5.2
-> Say her name again and I'll measure you.
    Halvard: The Warden's voice. She taught you that too. Keep it. You'll need it.
-> ...
    Halvard: Silence is not a plea. I'll enter it as one.
Halvard: The lamp you lit is Guild property. So is the map in your head.
Halvard: Surrender the pages at Halden and you're a journeyman again. Keep them and you're a hunt.
-> Then I'm a hunt.
    Halvard: Noted. Four paces, now. I've measured your reach.
-> What's the price of a licence?
    Halvard: Everything you've drawn since the Edge. You'll hear that offer once more. Not from me.
-> ...
    Halvard: Entered. The reeds carry it to Halden faster than I can.
Halvard: Halden, or before. The lance keeps its own count.
<<flag act1.halvard_met 1>>
<<flag act1.unlicensed 1>>
===

title: Lighthouse_Halvard_Idle
---
Halvard: Four paces. #still
===
